# 🚨 MEGA FRONTEND GENERATION PROMPT TEMPLATE

### 1️⃣ Project Name & Tagline

Write the project name and a one-line description.

---

### 2️⃣ Project Overview

Explain in 4-6 lines:

* what problem it solves
* who uses it
* what platform (web/PWA)
* any unique requirement (drag-drop / real-time / etc.)

---

### 3️⃣ Tech Stack

List:

* Framework (React)
* TypeScript
* Styling (CSS modules / No Tailwind)
* State (Zustand)
* Testing (Jest)

---

### 4️⃣ Engine Split

Divide the frontend into 4–12 **independent engines**, each with:

* clear responsibility
* isolated logic
* their own state
* their own tests

Examples (pick your own):

* UI Engine
* Canvas/Editor Engine
* Components Engine
* Auth/UI Guard Engine
* Undo/Redo Engine
* Offline/Cache Engine
* Routing Engine

---

### 5️⃣ Task Breakdown

For each engine:

* split into small tasks
* each task must include:

  * purpose
  * expected behavior
  * test cases

---

### 6️⃣ Code Generation Rules (short)

Tell the generator:

* write tests first
* then write code to pass them
* no TODOs / no placeholders
* no skipped logic
* real working React/TS code
* responsive + accessible

---

### 7️⃣ Integration Rules

After isolated engines are built:

* integrate them
* run integration tests
* ensure state + routing + UI works together

---

### 8️⃣ Output Order

The generator must output in this sequence:

1. engines definition
2. tasks
3. test files
4. implementation
5. integration
6. final build

---

### 📌 FINAL INSTRUCTION

```
Generate the entire frontend codebase engine-by-engine.
Use test-driven development.
Do not skip logic or features.
Produce real working TypeScript + React code.
Integrate all engines at the end.
```
